There is one. The relevant part of movemon(), not-directly-relevant
comment omitted:

        if (Conflict && !mtmp->iswiz && mtmp->mcansee) {
            if (couldsee(mtmp->mx,mtmp->my) &&
                (distu(mtmp->mx,mtmp->my) <= BOLT_LIM*BOLT_LIM) &&
                                                        fightm(mtmp))
                continue;       /* mon might have died */
        }
        if(dochugw(mtmp))               /* otherwise just move the monster */
            continue;

That is, the couldsee() check (and the distance check) will
short-circuit the monster-consider-fighting-monster call if they
fail. (couldsee() means that only line of sight is taken into account;
cansee() would consider lighting conditions as well.)

